    "pronunciation": {
      "body": "The ​reconstructed ‌pronunciation ‌of ​the ​name is ​**/yuhuang/** ​— ​Chinese ‌Reconstruction.[^1]\n\n​Phoneme ​by ‌phoneme:\n\n​- ‌**Y** ​— Initial ‌character ​of ​the ​restored ​form ​Yùhuáng.\n‌- ​**ùhuáng** ‌— Remainder ​of ‌the ​name, ‌preserving ​the ‌distinctive ​marks ​of ‌the ‌Chinese tradition.\n\n‌For ​the ​modern ‌speaker, ​the ​closest ‌approximation ​is: ​'YUHUANG' ‌— pronounce ​the ‌restored ​form ​with ​attention ​to ‌the ‌preserved ​diacritics ‌and length.\n\n​Kindred ​and ‌historical ‌forms ‌of ‌the ​name:\n\n‌- ​**Chinese** ​— Yùhuáng, ​the ‌restored ​Unicode ​form ​of ‌the ​name\n\n​Yùhuáng ​is Tier ‌1 ​because ‌the ​Chinese ‌form ​preserves ‌distinctive ‌features ​that ​ASCII loses: ​stress, ​length, ‌or ‌special ​characters.",
